+## 32. Configuring IntelliJ IDEA for Optimal Java Development (Windows, Mac, Linux)
+
+### The process 
+1. after intellig ide installed, open the ide 
+2. the ide automatically detect the jdk on pc 
+3. create new project window
+4. click on settings 
+   * you can change the light in appearence 
+   * editor -> general -> auto import 
+     * check true to `add unambiguous import on the fly`, `optimize imports on the fly`
+     * editor -> code folding : 
+       * deselect file header 
+       * deselect imports 
+       * deselect one-line method
+       * deselect clouseres
+       * deselect generic constructor 
+   * appearence : 
+     * check show line numbers 
+   * click ok
+5. click on projects 
